    <DataNode elementId="SHIKIMATE" textLabel="shikimate" type="Metabolite">
      <Xref identifier="JXOHGGNKMLTUBP-HSUXUTPPSA-M" dataSource="InChIKey" />
      <Graphics centerX="800" centerY="960" width="90.0" height="25.0" textColor="3955e7" fontName="Arial" fontWeight="Normal" fontStyle="Normal" fontDecoration="Normal" fontStrikethru="Normal" fontSize="12" hAlign="Center" vAlign="Middle" borderColor="3955e7" borderStyle="Solid" borderWidth="1.0" fillColor="FFFFFF" shapeType="Rectangle" />
      <Comment>|FRAME: SHIKIMATE &quot;Shikimate&quot;| is an important intermediate in the chorismate biosynthetic pathway. It was first isolated from Japanese star anise. Shikimate is used for the production of some antiviral drugs used to halt the spread of the flu virus, but as a biosynthetic intermediate, it is usually not found in high concentrations in organisms. Shikimate can be easily harvested from the needles of several species of pine trees, and biosynthetic pathways in |FRAME:TAX-562| have been enhanced to obtain sufficient amounts of the metabolite for commercial use.</Comment>
      <Property key="UniqueID" value="SHIKIMATE" />
